 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nThe colors of the time-of-use periods have the following meanings:\n\ne Orange blocks for off-peak rate periods (19:00 - 07:59 on weekdays)\n\ne Blue blocks for on-peak rate periods (08:00 - 18:59 on weekdays)\n\ne Green blocks for normal rate periods (all day on weekends and public holidays)\n\nThe consumption from each time-of-use period is aggregated and the quantities are valuated with different prices. This kind of rate\nmodel can be realized and billed in SAP IS-U using real-time pricing billing (RTP billing) or time-of-use billing (TOU billing).\n\nFor more information, see\nReal-Time Pricing Billing\nTime-of-Use Billing\n\nWith time-of-use exception programs and the occurrence of time-of-use exceptions, a dynamic element is added. The following\nfigure shows the same time-of-use rate as above. However, two time-of-use exceptions occurred within the period.\n\nOff-Peak Rate\n\nOn-Peak Rate\nTOU Exception\n\nWeekdays:\n\n19:00 \u2014 07:59:                 q2ct\n08:00 \u2014 18:59:                30ct\nWeekends/Public Holidays:\nEntire Day:               16ct\nTime-of-Use\n\nException Program\n\nTime-of-Use Exceptions:\n13.07. 12:30-15:00\n2207. 11:45-\u201414:30\n\nTime-of-Use Rate with Time-of-Use Exceptions\n\nThe time-of-use exceptions are highlighted in red and in the example they occurred on the 13th July, 12:30 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. and on\nthe 22nd July, 11:45 to 2:30 p.m.\n\nConditional billing takes the time-of-use exceptions into account and uses a special conditional rate for these exception periods.\n\nPrerequisites\n\nThe prerequisites for processing time-of-use exceptions and conditional billing are as follows:\n\ne Consumption data in the form of time series\n",
